#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:-1
msgid "Guide to the Krita community."
msgstr "Príručka ku komunite Krita"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:10
msgid "community"
msgstr "komunita"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:10
msgid "communication"
msgstr "komunikácia"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:16
msgid "The Krita Community"
msgstr "Komunita Krita"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:18
msgid ""
"Get in touch! Apart from the website at https://www.krita.org, the Krita "
"project has several main communication channels:"
msgstr ""
"Spojte sa s nami! Okrem webovej stránky na https://www.krita.org má projekt "
"Krita niekoľko hlavných komunikačných kanálov:"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:20
msgid "Internet Relay Chat (IRC)"
msgstr "Internet Relay Chat"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:21
msgid "The mailing list"
msgstr "Mailing list"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:22
#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:80
msgid "GitLab (KDE Invent)"
msgstr "GitLab (KDE Invent)"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:23
#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:96
msgid "Phabricator"
msgstr "Phabricator"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:24
msgid "Krita Artists community forum"
msgstr "Komunitné fórum Krita Artists"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:26
msgid ""
"While Krita developers and users are present on social media such as "
"Twitter, Mastodon, Reddit, Google+, Tumblr or Facebook, those are not the "
"place where we discuss new features, bugs, development or where we make "
"plans for the future."
msgstr ""
"Hoci vývojári a používatelia Krity sú prítomní na sociálnych sieťach ako "
"Twitter, Mastodon, Reddit, Google+, Tumblr alebo Facebook, to nie sú miesta, "
"kde diskutujeme o nových funkciách, chybách, vývoji alebo kde plánujeme "
"budúcnosť."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:28
msgid "There are also the:"
msgstr "Sú tu aj:"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:30
msgid "bug tracker"
msgstr "bug tracker"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:31
msgid "development sprints"
msgstr "vývojové šprinty"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:33
msgid ""
"You’ll find that there are a number of people are almost always around: the "
"core team."
msgstr "Zistíte, že niekoľko ľudí je takmer vždy k dispozícii: základný tím."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:35
msgid ""
"Halla (irc: halla): project maintainer, lead developer. Works full-time on "
"Krita. Manages the Krita Foundation, triages bugs, does social media and "
"admin stuff."
msgstr ""
"Halla (irc: halla): správca projektu, vedúci vývojár. Pracuje na Krite na "
"plný úväzok. Spravuje Nadáciu Krita, triedi chyby, stará sa o sociálne siete "
"a administráciu."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:36
msgid "Dmitry (irc: dmitryK|log): lead developer. Works full-time on Krita."
msgstr ""
"Dmitry (irc: dmitryK|log): vedúci vývojár. Pracuje na Krite na plný úväzok."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:37
msgid ""
"Wolthera (irc: Wolthera_laptop): developer, writes the manual and tutorials, "
"triages bugs, helps people out. Works full-time on Krita."
msgstr ""
"Wolthera (irc: Wolthera_laptop): vývojárka, píše príručku a návody, triedi "
"chyby, pomáha ľuďom. Pracuje na Krite na plný úväzok."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:38
msgid "Ivan Yossi (irc: ivanyossi|log): developer. Works full-time on Krita."
msgstr ""
"Ivan Yossi (irc: ivanyossi|log): vývojár. Pracuje na Krite na plný úväzok."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:39
msgid ""
"Agata Cacko (irc: tiar): developer, user supporter. Works full-time on "
"Krita. Also on reddit as u/-tiar- ."
msgstr ""
"Agata Cacko (irc: tiar): vývojárka, podpora používateľov. Pracuje na Krite "
"na plný úväzok. Tiež na reddite ako u/-tiar- ."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:40
msgid ""
"Emmet O'Neil (irc: emmetpdx): developer, works mostly on animation. Works "
"full-time on Krita."
msgstr ""
"Emmet O'Neil (irc: emmetpdx): vývojár, pracuje najmä na animácii. Pracuje na "
"Krite na plný úväzok."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:41
msgid "Scott Petrovic (irc: scottyp): UX designer, developer, webmaster."
msgstr "Scott Petrovic (irc: scottyp): UX dizajnér, vývojár, webmaster."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:42
msgid ""
"David Revoy (irc: deevad): expert user, creates Pepper & Carrot, maintains "
"the preset bundle."
msgstr ""
"David Revoy (irc: deevad): expertný používateľ, tvorí Pepper & Carrot, "
"spravuje balík predvolieb."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:43
msgid "Alvin Wong (irc: windragon): windows guru."
msgstr "Alvin Wong (irc: windragon): guru pre Windows."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:44
msgid "Ben Cooksley (irc: bcooksley): KDE system administrator."
msgstr "Ben Cooksley (irc: bcooksley): správca systémov KDE."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:46
msgid ""
"Krita’s team spans the globe, but most development happens in Europe and "
"Russia."
msgstr ""
"Tím Krity pokrýva celý svet, ale väčšina vývoja sa odohráva v Európe a Rusku."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:48
msgid ""
"Krita is part of the larger KDE community. The KDE® Community is a free "
"software community dedicated to creating an open and user-friendly computing "
"experience, offering an advanced graphical desktop, a wide variety of "
"applications for communication, work, education and entertainment and a "
"platform to easily build new applications upon. The KDE contributors guide "
"is relevant for Krita contributors, too, and can be found `here <https://"
"archive.flossmanuals.net/kde-guide/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Krita je súčasťou širšej komunity KDE. Komunita KDE® je komunita slobodného "
"softvéru venovaná vytváraniu otvoreného a užívateľsky prívetivého "
"výpočtového prostredia, ktorá ponúka pokročilú grafickú plochu, širokú škálu "
"aplikácií na komunikáciu, prácu, vzdelávanie a zábavu a platformu na "
"jednoduché budovanie nových aplikácií. Sprievodca pre prispievateľov KDE je "
"relevantný aj pre prispievateľov Krity a možno ho nájsť `tu <https://archive."
"flossmanuals.net/kde-guide/>`_."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:50
msgid ""
"The Krita Foundation was created to support development of Krita. The Krita "
"Foundation has sponsored Dmitry’s work on Krita since 2013."
msgstr ""
"Nadácia Krita bola vytvorená na podporu vývoja Krity. Nadácia Krita "
"sponzoruje prácu Dmitryho na Krite od roku 2013."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:55
msgid "Internet Relay Chat"
msgstr "Internet Relay Chat"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:57
msgid ""
"IRC is the main communication channel. There are IRC clients for every "
"operating system out there, as well as a web client on the krita website."
msgstr ""
"IRC je hlavný komunikačný kanál. Existujú IRC klienti pre každý operačný "
"systém, ako aj webový klient na webovej stránke krity."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:59
msgid ""
"Joining IRC: connect to Libera.Chat, select a unique nickname and join the "
"#krita and ##krita-chat channels. #krita is for on-topic talk, ##krita-chat "
"for off-topic chat."
msgstr ""
"Pripojenie k IRC: pripojte sa k Libera.Chat, vyberte jedinečnú prezývku a "
"pripojte sa ku kanálom #krita a ##krita-chat. #krita je na témy k veci, "
"##krita-chat na mimotémový rozhovor."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:60
msgid "Don’t ask to ask: if you’ve got a question, just ask it."
msgstr ""
"Nepýtajte sa, či sa môžete opýtať: ak máte otázku, jednoducho sa opýtajte."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:61
msgid ""
"Don’t panic if several discussions happen at the same time. That’s normal in "
"a busy channel."
msgstr ""
"Nepanikárte, ak prebieha viacero diskusií súčasne. To je normálne v rušnom "
"kanáli."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:62
msgid "Talk to an individual by typing their nick and a colon."
msgstr "Oslovte jednotlivca napísaním jeho prezývky a dvojbodky."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:63
msgid ""
"Almost every Monday, at 16:00 CET or CEST, we have a meeting where we "
"discuss what happened in the past week, what we’re doing, and everything "
"that’s relevant for the project. The meeting notes are kept in google docs."
msgstr ""
"Takmer každý pondelok o 16:00 SEČ alebo SELČ máme stretnutie, kde "
"diskutujeme o tom, čo sa stalo minulý týždeň, čo robíme, a o všetkom, čo je "
"relevantné pre projekt. Záznamy zo stretnutí sa uchovávajú v google docs."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:64
msgid ""
"Activity is highest in CET or CEST daytime and evenings. US daytime and "
"evenings are most quiet."
msgstr ""
"Aktivita je najvyššia počas dňa a večerov v SEČ alebo SELČ. Americké dni a "
"večery sú najkľudnejšie."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:65
msgid ""
"**IRC is not logged. If you close the channel, you will be gone, and you "
"will not be able to read what happened when you join the channel again. If "
"you ask a question, you have to stay around!**"
msgstr ""
"**IRC sa nezaznamenáva. Ak zatvoríte kanál, odídete a nebudete môcť čítať, "
"čo sa stalo, keď sa opäť pripojíte ku kanálu. Ak položíte otázku, musíte "
"zostať!**"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:66
msgid ""
"It is really irritating for other users and disrupting to conversations if "
"you keep connecting and disconnecting."
msgstr ""
"Je to skutočne otravné pre ostatných používateľov a narúša to rozhovory, ak "
"sa neustále pripájate a odpájate."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:70
msgid "Mailing List"
msgstr "Mailing List"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:72
msgid ""
"The mailing list is used for announcements and sparingly for discussions. "
"Everyone who wants to work on Krita one way or another should be subscribed "
"to the mailing list."
msgstr ""
"Poštový zoznam sa používa na oznámenia a sporadicky na diskusie. Každý, kto "
"chce pracovať na Krite akýmkoľvek spôsobom, by mal byť prihlásený na odber "
"poštového zoznamu."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:74
msgid ""
"`Mailing List Archives <https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/kimageshop>`_"
msgstr ""
"`Archívy poštového zoznamu <https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/"
"kimageshop>`_"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:76
msgid ""
"The mailing list is called \"kimageshop\", because that is the name under "
"which the Krita project was started. Legal issues (surprise!) led to two "
"renames, once to Krayon, then to Krita."
msgstr ""
"Poštový zoznam sa volá \"kimageshop\", pretože to je meno, pod ktorým bol "
"projekt Krita spustený. Právne problémy (prekvapenie!) viedli k dvom "
"premenovaniam, raz na Krayon, potom na Krita."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:82
msgid "GitLab serves the following purposes for the Krita team:"
msgstr "GitLab slúži nasledovným účelom pre tím Krity:"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:84
msgid ""
"Reviewing volunteers' submissions through Merge Requests (MR) on `Graphics/"
"Krita`_ for the code and `Documentation/Krita.org Documentation Website`_ "
"for the content of the Krita Manual."
msgstr ""
"Prezeranie príspevkov dobrovoľníkov prostredníctvom žiadostí o zlúčenie (MR) "
"na `Graphics/Krita`_ pre kód a `Documentation/Krita.org Documentation "
"Website`_ pre obsah príručky Krita."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:85
msgid ""
"Host the code git repository: https://invent.kde.org/graphics/krita.git . "
"Note that while there are mirrors of our git repository on Github and "
"Phabricator, we do not use them for Krita development."
msgstr ""
"Hostuje git repozitár kódu: https://invent.kde.org/graphics/krita.git . "
"Všimnite si, že hoci existujú zrkadlá nášho git repozitára na Github a "
"Phabricator, nepoužívame ich na vývoj Krity."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:86
msgid ""
"Host the Krita Manual content repository: https://invent.kde.org/"
"documentation/docs-krita-org"
msgstr ""
"Hostuje repozitár obsahu príručky Krita: https://invent.kde.org/"
"documentation/docs-krita-org"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:91
msgid "**Do not** make new issues on GitLab or use it to make bug reports."
msgstr ""
"**Nevytvárajte** nové problémy na GitLabe ani ho nepoužívajte na hlásenie "
"chýb."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:93
msgid ""
"**Do** put all your code submissions (merge requests) on GitLab. **Do not** "
"attach patches to bugs in the bug tracker."
msgstr ""
"**Ukladajte** všetky svoje kódové príspevky (žiadosti o zlúčenie) na GitLab. "
"**Nepripájajte** záplaty k chybám v sledovači chýb."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:98
msgid "Phabricator serves the following purposes for the Krita team:"
msgstr "Phabricator slúži nasledovným účelom pre tím Krity:"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:100
msgid ""
"Track what we are working on: https://phabricator.kde.org/maniphest/ This "
"includes development tasks, designing new features and UX design, as well as "
"tasks related to the website."
msgstr ""
"Sledovanie toho, na čom pracujeme: https://phabricator.kde.org/maniphest/ "
"Zahŕňa to vývojové úlohy, navrhovanie nových funkcií a UX dizajn, ako aj "
"úlohy súvisiace s webovou stránkou."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:102
msgid ""
"**Do not** report bugs as tasks on Phabricator. Phabricator is where we "
"organize our work."
msgstr ""
"**Nehlaste** chyby ako úlohy na Phabricatore. Phabricator je miesto, kde "
"organizujeme svoju prácu."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:105
msgid "Krita Artists"
msgstr "Krita Artists"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:107
msgid ""
"`Krita Artists <https://krita-artists.org>`_ is a forum built for users and "
"artists. Most of the developers have accounts on the forum too."
msgstr ""
"`Krita Artists <https://krita-artists.org>`_ je fórum vytvorené pre "
"používateľov a umelcov. Väčšina vývojárov má tiež účty na fóre."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:110
msgid "Bugzilla: the Bug Tracker"
msgstr "Bugzilla: Bug Tracker"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:112
msgid ""
"Krita shares the bug tracker with the rest of the KDE community. Krita bugs "
"are found under the Krita product. There are two kinds of reports in the bug "
"tracker: bugs and wishes. See the chapters on :ref:`Bug Reporting "
"<bugs_reporting>` and :ref:`Bug Triaging <triaging_bugs>` on how to handle "
"bugs. Wishes are feature requests. Do not report feature requests in "
"bugzilla unless a developer has asked you to. See the chapter on :ref:"
"`Feature Requests <developing_features>` for what is needed to create a good "
"feature request."
msgstr ""
"Krita zdieľa sledovač chýb so zvyškom komunity KDE. Chyby Krity sa "
"nachádzajú pod produktom Krita. V sledovači chýb sú dva druhy hlásení: chyby "
"a želania. Pozrite si kapitoly o :ref:`Hlásení chýb <bugs_reporting>` a :ref:"
"`Triedení chýb <triaging_bugs>` ohľadom spracovania chýb. Želania sú "
"žiadosti o funkcie. Nehlaste žiadosti o funkcie v bugzille, pokiaľ vás o to "
"nepožiadal vývojár. Pozrite si kapitolu o :ref:`Žiadostiach o funkcie "
"<developing_features>` pre informácie o tom, čo je potrebné na vytvorenie "
"dobrej žiadosti o funkciu."

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:115
msgid "Sprints"
msgstr "Šprinty"

#: ../../contributors_manual/community.rst:117
msgid ""
"Sometimes, core Krita developers and users come together, most often in "
"Deventer, the Netherlands, to work together on our code design, UX design, "
"the website or whatever needs real, face-to-face contact. Travel to sprints "
"is usually funded by KDE e.V., while accommodation is funded by the Krita "
"Foundation."
msgstr ""
"Niekedy sa základní vývojári a používatelia Krity stretnú, najčastejšie v "
"Deventer v Holandsku, aby spoločne pracovali na dizajne kódu, UX dizajne, "
"webovej stránke alebo na čomkoľvek, čo vyžaduje skutočný, osobný kontakt. "
"Cestovanie na šprinty zvyčajne financuje KDE e.V., zatiaľ čo ubytovanie "
"financuje Nadácia Krita."

